    "summary": "dsh-univer-office@0.3.5 is a DSH Web-plane plugin: its manifest declares dsh.client.platform=web with client UI injections, and the README installs it with `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-univer-office` then restarts with `dsh web`. No SDK, ACP, headless, or TUI workflow is documented, so executionProfiles is web only; the bundled headless Unit Content Worker is an internal component, not a DSH headless run path. Node intent: engines.node is >=22.19.0 in both source and published manifests, and CI configures node@22 (ci.yml `runtime: node@22`, release.yml `node-version: 22`), so major 22 is selected as ci-tested and satisfies the declared engine minimum; no author-recommended major beyond that was found. Development tooling is pinned as pnpm@11.23.0 via packageManager and the README development section; this is a development-scope fact and no consumer-profile package manager requirement is documented. The README names three supported DSH baselines (0.1.5-rc.3, 0.1.7-alpha.2, 0.1.7-rc.1); the target 0.1.7-rc.2 is not among them, though the peer range ^0.1.7-rc.1 nominally admits it. This recommendation records author intent only and does not prove compatibility.",
